# `builtin:exec`

Runs a command on the host when the step starts, and optionally another command on teardown.

```cue
migrate: {
    uses: "builtin:exec"
    with: {
        up:   {command: ["./scripts/migrate.sh", "up"]}
        down: {command: ["./scripts/migrate.sh", "down"]}
    }
}
```

To send the commands' requests through the kevin proxy:

```cue
fetch: {
    uses: "builtin:exec"
    with: {
        up:     {command: ["curl", "-fsSL", "-o", "/tmp/asset.tar.gz", "https://example.com/asset.tar.gz"]}
        proxy:  true
        egress: ["example.com"]
    }
}
```

For a tool that takes a CA file or proxy address only as a flag, use the [`project`]({{< relref "/docs/reference/cel-expressions#project" >}}) variables:

```cue
up: command: [
    "curl", "--cacert", "${project.root_cert}",
    "--proxy", "${project.http_proxy_addr}",
    "https://internal.example.com",
]
```

